[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Vp4j0xDR/DTXSyzN4"]
[FEN "r4rk1/pbpp2pp/1p2q3/5n2/1nPP1B2/2NQ1PPB/PP5P/2KR3R w - - 1 15"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r4rk1/pbpp2pp/1p2q3/5n2/1nPP1B2/2NQ1PPB/PP5P/2KR3R_w_-_-_1_15"]

{ His king sits on c1 and his light bishop is far away on h3. Which colour is weak around his king? }
15. Qf1 { His queen steps to f1, tucking in behind his own king. Where do you send yours? } 15... Qg6 { Queen to g6: out of harm's way, and it stares down the diagonal at b1. [%cal Gg6b1][%csl Gg6] } (15... Qf6 { Aiming at two pawns, and the knight on b4 is left hanging. } 16. a3 g5 17. Be5 { The knight is trapped. Lost. [%csl Rb4] }) (15... g5 { You poke the bishop, and he pokes your knight. } 16. a3 gxf4 17. axb4 { A messy trade. Equal. }) (15... Ba6 { The bishop hits a rook, and nothing happens. } 16. b3 g5 17. a3 { Your knight is in trouble now. Worse. [%csl Rb4] }) (15... a5 { You guard the knight, but the queen was the point. } 16. a3 g5 17. d5 { He is better now. }) (15... Bxf3 { A free pawn? The queen takes back and hits your knight. } 16. Qxf3 g5 17. a3 { A piece is lost. [%csl Rb4,Rf5] }) 16. Bxf5 { He trades the bishop. Take back with the queen. } 16... Qxf5 { The queen sits on f5, on the light squares, staring at his king. [%csl Gf5][%cal Gf5b1] } (16... Rxf5 { The rook takes, and the queen loses her diagonal. } 17. Rd2 Qf7 18. d5 { His centre rolls and your queen is off the diagonal. Worse. [%csl Rf5] }) 17. Rd2 { He covers c2. Now hit the bishop. } 17... g5 { The pawn kicks the bishop, and the f3 pawn falls next. [%cal Gg5f4,Gb7f3][%csl Rf3] } (17... d5 { A solid move, and his a pawn kicks your knight. } 18. a3 a5 19. axb4 axb4 { A mess. Equal. }) (17... a5 { You guard the knight and he breaks in the middle. } 18. d5 c6 19. dxc6 Bxc6 { Equal: the centre opened up, and the trade left nothing for either side to grab. }) (17... Rae8 { The rook waits, and the knight is kicked. } 18. d5 d6 19. a3 { The knight has to go home. Slightly worse. [%csl Rb4] }) (17... d6 { Slow, and his pawns roll. } 18. h4 a5 19. a3 { Worse: a3 kicks the knight and you have not started anything on the king side yet. }) 0-1


[Event "Strategy: the weak colour, the light squares"]
